;; orphan_wiki_pages — wiki pages connected to nothing (REQ-KG-006).
;;
;; Booklogic port of assets/queries/coverage/orphan_wiki_pages.rq:
;;   SELECT ?page WHERE {
;;     ?page a tbf:WikiPage .
;;     FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?claim tbf:hasSourceSpan ?page . }
;;     FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?chapter tbf:referencesPage ?page . }
;;   }
;;
;; The :where binds every projected wiki page id (one row per wiki/**/*.md file,
;; minted to the SAME URI project_graph emits for tbf:WikiPage). The two :not
;; arms are the two FILTER NOT EXISTS clauses:
;;   - no source span cites the page (source-span/wiki-page-id = ?page), i.e. no
;;     claim has the page as its hasSourceSpan target; and
;;   - no chapter references the page (chapter-wiki-ref/wiki-page-id = ?page).
;; Both negations join on the already-bound ?page, so they lower to safe Cozo
;; negations. A page surviving both is connected to nothing -> an orphan.
(defquery :orphan-wiki-pages
  :find  [?page]
  :where [[?p :wiki-page/id ?page]]
  :not   [[?s :source-span/wiki-page-id ?page]
          [?r :chapter-wiki-ref/wiki-page-id ?page]])
